Washington DC is a unique student city — politics and policy are the local industry, free museums line the National Mall, and the metro system is clean and reliable. Rent is high but concentrated in certain areas; students who know where to look can find genuine value.

### Georgetown University

**Georgetown**: Walking distance but very expensive. No Metro stop (by design — residents fought it). Rooms USD 1,200–2,000/month.

**Rosslyn (Arlington, VA)**: Across the Key Bridge. 15 min walk to Georgetown, Blue/Orange/Silver Line Metro. Rooms USD 900–1,600/month.

**Glover Park**: North of Georgetown, 10 min walk. More residential. Rooms USD 1,000–1,700/month.

### GWU (Foggy Bottom)

**Foggy Bottom**: Right at campus, between the White House and the Kennedy Center. Expensive. Rooms USD 1,200–2,200/month.

**Columbia Heights**: 10 min Green Line. Vibrant Latino community on 14th Street, gentrified with excellent food. Rooms USD 900–1,600/month.

**Petworth**: Further north on the Green Line. Rapidly changing with new restaurants and bars. Rooms USD 800–1,400/month.

### American University (Tenleytown)

**Tenleytown & Friendship Heights**: Walking distance to AU. Quiet, safe, near Rock Creek Park. Rooms USD 900–1,600/month.

**Van Ness & Cleveland Park**: 1–2 Red Line stops south of AU. Connecticut Avenue corridor. Rooms USD 900–1,600/month.

### Value Zone: NoVA & Maryland Suburbs

**Arlington & Alexandria (VA)**: Across the Potomac, on multiple Metro lines. Pentagon City, Crystal City, and Old Town Alexandria have good student apartments. Rooms USD 800–1,400/month.

**Silver Spring & Takoma Park (MD)**: Northern suburbs on the Red Line. Silver Spring has a revitalized downtown; Takoma Park is crunchy and progressive. Rooms USD 700–1,300/month.

### FAQ

**How important is the Metro?** Essential. Live within 10 min walk of a station. DC's Metro is one of the few US systems that people actually rely on.
**Is DC cheaper than NYC/Boston?** Slightly cheaper than Boston for student housing, much cheaper than NYC — but still expensive by national standards.
**Best budget tip?** Group houses. Large DC row houses with 4–6 bedrooms can bring individual rent down to USD 700–1,000/month in areas like Petworth or Brookland.
